Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||05-24-2001||03:39 AM||||Don't get me wrong, I'm a huge Star Trek fan, but I never really cared much for both Voyager or DS9... I dislike Voyager for several reasons. First and foremost because Voyager (the series) was breaking all kinds of rules set for the <I>Star Trek universe</I>. For instance, in the first episode, the Voyager was introduced as a <B>battle</B>ship, while it was made very clear in STTOS and STTNG that the human part of the Federation doesn't have any battleships. Another good example was the episode where they found a way to reach warp 10 - and even exceeded it. Another impossibility in the Star Trek universe. Or where they <B>landed</B> Voyager on a planet's surface. If Rodenberry was still alive, he most certainly would have never allowed that to happen.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And of course there is Janeway. How she ever became captain of a starship is beyond me.<P>DS9 wouldn't be bad if they didn't try to make Sisko the most important man in the universe.<P>"Gene Luck Pickerd? Is there a Gene Luck Pickerd here?"<p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||05-24-2001||03:57 AM||||I wasn't clear on one thing about the Borg.. they never said when, during the time frame of the 24th century, did they go back for the events in First Contact.. couldn't have been the same queen. oh well..<P>anyway, I'm looking forward to the new series.. it starts next fall, right?<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000009||bHooper||05-24-2001||08:05 AM||||awwwww... shiite!  i cant believe i missed it!<P>dont tell me i dont want to know.<P>i had heard about that scott backula fella gonna be a captain, it seems just as strange as hercules comanding a ship!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000010||LZeitgeist||05-24-2001||08:50 AM||||What I'd like to know is, since the Borg had that big "array" (you know what I mean if you saw the show), why didn't they just wipe Earth off the map a long time ago?<P>Granted, I haven't watched Voyager in about three years (except when I'd find a scene with Seven in it while surfing through channels <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">), so I'm sure there's a lot I've missed, but that was one of the questions that popped up in my mind as I was watching it last night...||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fiero5||05-24-2001||08:58 AM||||I am a big Star Trek fan. I can remember coming home from school and trying to get the roof entenna turned to bring in channel 56 so I could watch it at 4pm. More days than not it would come in crappy. I would yell down to my poor Dad as soon as he got home, asking if he could help me get the channel in better. This would usually require him to go up on the roof and help turn the entenna. My father and I would watch Looney tunes on Saturday mornings and would watch Star Trek each weekday together. That was pretty cool!<P>I have a huge Satr Trek collection that takes up most our bedroom. I focus mostly on the original series for collection. Toys that were out when I was kid, from like 1971 to 1979. 1974 and 1976 had the best Star Trek toys I think.<P>I found this last Voyager episode entertaining, but I tire of the going back in time stuff. <BR>The part I thought was the dumbest, was when the Batmobile shields went up over Voyager.<BR>I yelled out "Give me a break!".<P>Also, the borg exploded as soon as the transwarp torpedoes hit the cube ships.<BR>It realy should have been a few seconds or more, as the torpedoe impacted into the cube and did lots of internal damage before the whole ship would explode. In First contact they bombarded a section for awhile to get thru all that ship. The Borg cubes are very large inside as we saw in the opening pull back shot in First Contact.<P>The teaser about the new Star Trek this fall was interesting:<P>"Before there was Janeway....before there was Pickard...before there was Spock...there was Enterprise."  Ooooh.<P>Anyway, just my two pennies on the subject.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero1sig.JPG">                   <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
Z||000012||LZeitgeist||05-24-2001||09:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>The teaser about the new Star Trek this fall was interesting:<P>"Before there was Janeway....before there was Pickard...before there was Spock...there was Enterprise." Ooooh.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>(Actually, you forgot Kirk after Spock, but that's O.K...)<P>When I saw that, I went down the list in my head, and I noticed they left out Sisko... I'm sure Avery Brooks was just *thrilled* to have been left completely out...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cheever2||05-24-2001||10:25 AM||||Like all my friends, I watched Star Trek when I was young.  Loved it, but then again, I liked <B><I>It's About Time</I></B>.  Anyways, I have never been able to stomach any of the spinoff shows.  Sorry to be a sourpuss in your space-post, but just wanted you to know that there is somebody who doesn't like those shows.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Pontiaddict||05-24-2001||11:57 AM||||I get to see alot of Voyager and Next Generation reruns and you can pick apart either rather easily and find many, lets call them, irregularities. As far as the original Star Trek, there are about 5 episodes that I can actually stand.<BR>I'm really not looking forward to Enterprise either. to do it right, they will have to make everything tackier than the original Star Trek, or make it look decent and totally unbelieveable, plus, they are going to discover a bunch of alien races that most Star Trek viewers already know about. It seems boring to me.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||12:09 PM||||Voyagers final episode: <P>Fiizzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzz. snap!<P>  time travel - the universal solution to anyproblem - we can always go back one day sooner and try again!<P>  I though it was very un-imaginative to completely wipe out the Borg like that - they just killed off what? a trillion living beings?<P>   are we still living with the 20th century philosophy of, if you cant get along with em, nuke em?||||reg||1
