Z||000020||LZeitgeist||05-24-2001||02:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>are we still living with the 20th century philosophy of, if you cant get along with em, nuke em?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, sure! Has there ever been a philosophy *other* than that one?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Never seen a "Peace, Love and Assimilation" bumper sticker...||||reg||1
Z||000021||Fiero5||05-24-2001||02:20 PM||||Well, part of Star Trek's problem in the last years is that "the great bird of the galaxy" is no longer around to steer the franchise ship. Especially when those who are in charge of it now (Rick Berman) want to go right when they should go left.<P>Having said that, I think that learning how we first met the Andorians and such would be pretty cool. Look at how the Klingons changed in the first movie and how they handled that in the "Tribble" sequel of DS9. Worf's statement to his fellow crewmen at the table at K-7 was priceless.<P>I think that true Star Trek fans will overlook what obviously has to be done in situations like this as long as it is well done and not just "thrown in".<P>Just think, they could show earlier federation ships before the constitution class was created, which the U.S.S. Enterprise was the flag ship of.<P>I wonder if they will use the early pre-production sketches that you see in the various making of Star Trek books as early versions of the ship?<BR>That would be cool.<P>I would like to add that I don't believe they "destroyed" the Borg, only some of them when they crushed the network holes that allowed the Borg to move thru out the galaxy in short periods of time. This was a nice touch to explain why we seem to see the Borg everywhere, including in the Delta Quadrant.<P>As for now not having to see "Voyager: The movie", that is actually a good possibility now. Just as TNG has/had their own run of Star Trek movies following the original crews final stand in "The Undiscovered Country".<BR>Though I think DS9 will probably have first shot of the next Satr Trek movie seires as there run ended before Voyagers.<BR>Maybe they could have Voyager be one of the ships commissioned to help DS( in the movie?<BR>Who knows.<P>We will just have to sit back and waite I guess.<P>Steve<P><P>------------------<BR>                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero9signature.jpg">                    <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||9
Z||000022||thomas_l||05-24-2001||02:30 PM||||The only low spot is that its easy to see that this episode was typical: 1.75 hours of buildup that could have one of two possible outcomes then 15 minutes to wrap it up. That way if they decided at the last minute to go another season they only have to re-shoot the last 10% of the episode. At least we got to see the whole 2 hours since they killed the series. Otherwise you get the first hour for a teaser then have to wait until fall to see part 2. I HATE THAT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||8
