Z||000026||Fformula88||05-24-2001||07:51 PM||||I think they would have been better off making their homecoming a "movie".  The larger budget would have led to better and more battle scenes, and hopefully a better storyline as well.<P>As for "Enterprise", I cannot imagine how the bridge is going to look.  How do you fit it in before the original series without making the bridge look cheesier than the original!  <P>Also, did anyone hear that the actress that plays Janeway is VERY upset that they didn't make the captain in Enterprise another female?  The federation must not have been as open to equal opportunity back in the 23rd century  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000027||c m west||05-24-2001||10:25 PM||||thats because "Enterprise" is going to take place only 100 years from now. Generalization is that its going to be NASA with new-fangled "warp technology" and those that are affraid to use the "new" transporter technology.<P>  I believe they will use a Deadulus class ship ( Im prolly one of the biggest trekkie and trekker one the forum )<P> We just became friends with the Vulcans and they are holding our hand as they are introducing us to space travel.<BR> To wrap it up... the new series will be before Janeway, Sisko, Picard, Garret(enterprise C ), Fuller ( enterprise B ), Kirk, and even Pike ( long before Kirk )<P> the slate doesnt get any cleaner than this - and the writers of "Endgame" can lick a hairy nutsack - they destroyed seven years of filming and writing in one hour and 45 minutes, all of which was far from creative.<P> What about meeting Kim's mom that he was always going on about - seeing Admiral Paris's reaction to his son shaping up - Janeway's love interest she left behind as well as her Irish Setter, 7 of 9 adapting to her new humanity and her home world, The former Maqius crew being pardoned - and the general homecoming party that happened when they got home - not the one from the previous timeline either, seeing as how that no longer exists<P> -- oh yeah - the batmobile sheilds really took alaot of thought too =-(<P> Eric - West Coast Fiero<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR> 310-305-4111||||reg||1
